This product contains default thresholds for its behaviour scenarios
(gateway/internal/behaviour, spec MVP-17: login_bruteforce, path_probing,
aggressive_crawl) that were adapted from scenarios of the CrowdSec Hub
(https://github.com/crowdsecurity/hub), namely crowdsecurity/http-bf-wordpress_bf,
crowdsecurity/http-generic-bf, crowdsecurity/http-probing and
crowdsecurity/http-crawl-non_statics. It also contains the virtual patching
rules of the CrowdSec Hub (collection crowdsecurity/appsec-virtual-patching,
spec MVP-26): a pinned snapshot in gateway/internal/hub/snapshot.json, whose
commit is recorded there and in gateway/internal/hub/snapshot.NOTICE, and at
runtime the rules of the public hub index. No CrowdSec software, scenario file,
parser or IP data is included or used at runtime, the CrowdSec engine does not
run, and nothing is sent to CrowdSec beyond the request for the public file.
